so let's talk about the senate huge  senate news  over the weekend according to the latest  update  from the non-partisan cook political  report democrats are now  slightly favored to take control of the  senate from republicans in november now  what does this mean for  us nothing everyone has to vote no  matter what is going on  but let's actually discuss so back in  2019  i didn't think democrats had a good shot  at taking the senate in 2020  um we have 100 senators every two years  one-third of them are up for re-election  and the third of the seats that were up  in 2020  were not in early 2019 looking very  favorable for democrats trump was  polling okay enough  that the incumbent republicans weren't  being hugely hurt and i did a story in  may of 2019 called  why democrats won't take the senate in  2020 and in the clip i say  this is the situation right now if  something changes i will update you  and then things sort of did change and  some seats started looking not quite so  good for incumbent republicans trump  wasn't doing so hot  and so by october of 2019 i did another  close analysis of each race each seat up  for re-election  and that got me to a point where i  revised my view  and told you in october of 2019  democrats could  take the senate in 2020. now  i've been following this closely for you  since and in may  of this year just a couple months ago i  did a story where  there was an uphill battle certainly but  a much clearer path for democrats to  take the senate and again i came back to  you on may 20th and i said  democrats could take the senate from  republicans and it was uphill but it was  a much more reasonable path  and things have now gotten so bad  for donald trump and incumbent  republicans even loosely associated with  him in the last two months since that  story that the cook political report  100 days out from this election now says  that democrats are favored to take back  the senate  now it's a slim margin but a slight edge  to democrats to take back the senate  is a dramatically different situation  than what we had 18 months ago now as a  reminder  right now the senate is 53 to 47  republicans over democrats of the 47  that i'm including on the democratic  side  it's actually 45 democrats plus two  independents  uh angus king and that guy bernie  sanders who are independents but caucus  with democrats that's where you get 47  democrats  and 53 republicans in july  five races changed in such a way that  the cook political report  changed their projection to a slight  edge  to democrats to control the senate the  changes in july  are in arizona martha mcsally  is losing pretty badly to mark kelly in  polls  and that has gone from a toss-up to  leaning democratic  in iowa joni ernst the incumbent  republican that race has gone from  leaning republican to a toss-up  in georgia david perdue's race has gone  from leaning republican to  a toss-up in minneapolis in minnesota  rather  tina smith went from likely democratic  victory to  solid democratic victory and then in new  mexico which is currently an open seat  uh it went from likely democrat tom  udall winning  to solidly democrat tom udall winning  now those are the changes in july  which have pushed the senate overall to  more likely to be taken control of by  democrats but  you've got a whole bunch of other races  that have not changed in july which  we've talked about colorado and north  carolina  are very vulnerable republican seats  that's cory gardner  and uh tom tillis uh those are leaning  democratic  in maine susan collins is in a real  uphill battle probably her toughest  re-election campaign  really ever i believe susan collins was  first elected don't hold me to this but  i believe 96  meaning she had re-election campaigns in  2002  2008 2014 that makes sense and 2020  all of her other re-election campaigns  have been not particularly challenging  for her and sarah gideon at least in  some polls recently is actually ahead so  maine a tough one for republicans to  hold and really  maine should not have a republican  senator we they should replace uh  susan collins as soon as possible we've  talked about montana where  democrat steve bullock is doing well he  could end up being senator from montana  there are question marks around seats in  kansas  texas alaska and south carolina so  there's a whole bunch of different  possibilities and the point of this  story is not about  analyzing each of them in extreme detail  but about the idea  that what looked you know in early 2019  the data was saying maybe democrats can  pick up a seat or two  but taking control would probably be  2022.  uh and 2022 doesn't even look that  obviously great depending on which  states you're looking at  it shifted to there's a path  but all these different maybes need to  go the way of the democratic  challengers it is now shifted to you  know there's more races leaning  democratic and now you don't need as  much of a performance  outside of what would be reasonable to  take control of the senate and so that's  how now it is being called a  slight edge for democrats in the cook  political report so  this is all a way of me telling you what  to stay home and say  other people got it no of course not  this is a way of me saying  hey here is an opportunity  which we will only seize if we all go  out and vote  ignore every poll and go out and vote if  you don't like the republican  senator that is representing your state  right now ignore the polls  and vote and we'll keep covering the  senate outlook and the  this is particularly important because  of the conversation we had at the top of  the show  if joe biden wins him doing stuff  that we want him to do is going to  depend hugely on having the senate in  the first two years in office  historically when the white house  changes hands  in an election year two years later in  those midterms  that party that took control of the  white house often suffers losses  in the house and or senate we don't want  that  but what we can do in the immediate is  let's give joe biden if he were to win  a senate that is democratically  controlled and a house that is  democratically controlled if that  happens  the two years between january 21st uh  january 20th  2021 and january 2023  may be the biggest opportunity for  progressive change  in decades in the united states well i  guess we would put it up there  with the couple years between 2009 and  2011 when barack obama had the  opportunity  uh mishandled some things but also got  many things done  including obamacare so that's the  opportunity this is absolutely huge and  all you have to do is go vote you know  it can be overwhelming oh  tom udall and then martha mcsally and  all the  i can't focus on your scope of influence  focus on your sphere of influence which  is  am i allowed to vote oh i am because you  know i'm a citizen obviously  you can if you're if you're legally  voting then that's what you should do  i'm going to go and vote and that's all  i can control and then i can work on get  out the vote  and i can work on whatever else work on  what you can control and we have a real  opportunity here  real quick i want to tell you about our  sponsor magic spoon  who have done something awesome they've  taken all of our favorite sugary  childhood cereals  that we know we shouldn't eat anymore  and turn them into something you can  actually feel good about eating as an  adult there's four flavors  cocoa fruity frosted and blueberry they  taste great they're crunchy  they're sweet like you would expect this  type of cereal to be  but it's perfect for a ketogenic diet  because one bowl has only  three net carbs 12 grams of protein it's  sugar-free  gluten-free grain-free soy-free  once our team tried magic spoon for the  first time we actually ended up emailing  magic spoon back and saying can you send  us  more boxes send more samples they've  been a big hit  with david pakman show staffers and  magic spoon  knows how delicious their cereal is  because if you don't like it they'll  refund all of your money no questions  asked  and you'll get free shipping when you go  to magicspoon.com  pacman and use the code pacman that's  p-a-k-m-a-n

